   "source": [
    "# Pandas"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "078747dd-2fd1-462b-80d3-f10ae2f48217",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--> Definition : Pandas is a open source python library designed for data manipulation and analysis.\n",
    "--> open source : Code is also available for Free.\n",
    "\n",
    "--> Pandas is designed over Numpy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "6c33761e-d1f5-4e00-a267-3ed9d7ab3ce1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--> Important Operations in Pandas :\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Data Structures creation (Series, Dataframe)\n",
    "2. Data Input and Output (From CSV, Excel, SQL, JSON files)\n",
    "3. Understand the Dataset using pandas\n",
    "4. Data Filtering and Indexing (loc and iloc)\n",
    "5. Handling Missing Values (Null Values)\n",
    "6. Handling Duplicate values\n",
    "7. Handling Inconsistent Data\n",
    "8. Data Transformation using apply(), map()\n",
    "9. Aggregation and Grouping\n",
    "10. Time Series Data Generation\n",
    "11. Data Visualization"
   ]
  },
  {
